# =============================================================================
#  assets/textures/parts_farm.pix  —  the parts a farm person is made of
# =============================================================================
#  Three tiles, and none of them is a character. That is the point: a body, a head
#  and a hat compose into a cast, and the cast is bigger than the drawings. Two
#  colour swaps on the same two parts already give you a second person who is
#  obviously from the same village — which is the trade a parts mixer makes and a
#  brush cannot: you give up freedom and you get a family resemblance you would
#  otherwise have to draw by hand, sixty times, consistently.
#
#  Drawn here rather than taken from a pack because Kenney's Tiny Town is buildings
#  and terrain; it has no people in it. The skin and cloth tones are ours.
#
#  The body occupies rows 8..15 and the head rows 0..8, so both parts sit at 0,0 on
#  a 16x16 canvas and meet at the neck. A part's OFFSET is therefore usually zero,
#  and the composition is legible in the `.mix` file instead of hidden in arithmetic.
# =============================================================================
size 16
grid 3 1

palette . 00000000
palette f e8b891      # skin
palette n c99a76      # skin, in shadow at the neck
palette e 2b1d16      # eye
palette m a05a4a      # mouth
palette k 5b3a29      # hair   <- swapped for a second character
palette t 6e8fb5      # tunic  <- swapped for a second character
palette s 3f4a5a      # belt
palette p 4a4a55      # trousers
palette b 2e2e36      # shoes
palette h 8a5a3c      # hat

# ---- 0: the body -----------------------------------------------------------
tile 0
................
................
................
................
................
................
................
................
....tttttttt....
...tttttttttt...
...tttttttttt...
...tttttttttt...
....ssssssss....
....pp....pp....
....pp....pp....
....bb....bb....

# ---- 1: the head -----------------------------------------------------------
tile 1
.....kkkkkk.....
....kkkkkkkk....
....kffffffk....
....ffffffff....
....feffffef....
....ffffffff....
....fffmmfff....
.....ffffff.....
......nnnn......
................
................
................
................
................
................
................

# ---- 2: a hat, which is the whole argument in one tile ---------------------
#  Nobody drew "a person in a hat". The hat is a part, so every body and every head
#  already has a version wearing one, and the day there are four heads there are
#  four more characters for the price of nothing.
tile 2
................
